{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChJpEXeChDWhXsGUh7q9G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`ccode(sinc(x))` now produces valid C:\n\n```\n((x != 0) ? (\n   sin(x)/x\n)\n: (\n   1\n))\n```\n\n**Cause:** The C printer had no rule for `sinc`. It also had no rule for comparisons, so `Ne(x, 0)` printed as SymPy's own text (`Ne(x, 0)`) rather than as C.\n\n**Fix:** I added two methods to `sympy/printing/ccode.py`:\n- `_print_sinc` rewrites `sinc(x)` as `Piecewise((sin(x)/x, Ne(x, 0)), (1, True))` and prints that, which is what the issue suggested.\n- `_print_Relational` prints comparisons as `lhs op rhs`. So `Ne(x, 0)` becomes `x != 0`, and other comparisons like `x < 1` print as normal C operators too.\n\n**Testing:** The repro script now gives the output above. The tests in `test_ccode.py`, `test_codeprinter.py` and `test_codegen.py` all pass (83 tests). I didn't add new tests, because the rules don't allow editing test files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1667,"cache_read_input_tokens":19424,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1667},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7257831b-c4ea-48c5-adf0-f6d60b1abddb","uuid":"aef17262-7ad0-43dc-a030-bfcb7fb0bc65","timestamp":"2026-11-22T23:13:55.276Z","request_id":"req_011ChJpEXKqxGr8SopBNaDQS"}
